            <ArticleTitle>Direct Aziridination of Nitroalkenes Affording N-Alkyl-C-nitroaziridines and the Subsequent Lewis Acid Mediated Isomerization to β-Nitroenamines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5442-5445</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02724</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A mild and highly diastereoselective one-pot synthesis of trans-N-alkyl-C-nitroaziridines was achieved by treatment of nitroalkenes with aliphatic amines and N-chlorosuccinimide. Treatment of the obtained aziridines with a Lewis acid resulted in a facile ring opening reaction, accompanied by rearrangement and isomerization into functionalized (Z)-β-nitroenamines.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
